# Vulnerability details

## **Vulnerability Details:**

Operators select DSSs to allocate their funds to, and for each DSS, they can choose a list of vaults to stake. The [requestUpdateVaultStakeInDSS](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-karak/blob/f5e52fdcb4c20c4318d532a9f08f7876e9afb321/src/Core.sol#L130) function can be called by operators to stake a vault to a DSS they are registered to.

```solidity
    function requestUpdateVaultStakeInDSS(Operator.StakeUpdateRequest memory vaultStakeUpdateRequest)
        external
        nonReentrant
        whenFunctionNotPaused(Constants.PAUSE_CORE_REQUEST_STAKE_UPDATE)
        returns (Operator.QueuedStakeUpdate memory updatedStake)
    {
        address operator = msg.sender;
        CoreLib.Storage storage self = _self();
        self.checkIfOperatorIsRegInRegDSS(operator, vaultStakeUpdateRequest.dss);
        updatedStake = self.requestUpdateVaultStakeInDSS(vaultStakeUpdateRequest, self.nonce++, operator);
        emit RequestedStakeUpdate(updatedStake);
    }
```

This can then be finalized with the [finalizeUpdateVaultStakeInDSS](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-karak/blob/f5e52fdcb4c20c4318d532a9f08f7876e9afb321/src/Core.sol#L146) function after the MIN_STAKE_UPDATE_DELAY has passed, allowing the vault to be fully staked to the DSS.

```solidity
    function finalizeUpdateVaultStakeInDSS(Operator.QueuedStakeUpdate memory queuedStake)
        external
        nonReentrant
        whenFunctionNotPaused(Constants.PAUSE_CORE_FINALIZE_STAKE_UPDATE)
    {
        _self().validateAndUpdateVaultStakeInDSS(queuedStake);
        emit FinishedStakeUpdate(queuedStake);
    }
```

However, there is a scenario where a vault stake finalization can be executed to a DSS that is no longer registered to the operator. Since the check for the operator's registration is done only at the request stage, if an operator unregisters from the DSS, anyone can still call the finalizeUpdateVaultStakeInDSS function to finalize the stake of the operator's vault even though it is no longer registered.

This issue was identified and marked as “fixed” here:

- Issue M1: [https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-karak/blob/main/audits/core/Renascence - Karak Core Audit Report.pdf](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-karak/blob/main/audits/core/Renascence%20-%20Karak%20Core%20Audit%20Report.pdf)

However, the issue was not actually fixed. Furthermore, in the previously identified issue, the finalizeUpdateVaultStakeInDSS function was limited to only the operator. In the current code, it is open to be called by anyone, significantly increasing the chances of the problem occurring.

## **Impact:**

The impact is the same as mentioned when the issue was identified in the previous audit. The operator's state will indicate that there are staked funds towards the DSS for a particular vault that belongs to the operator. This could lead to the DSS handing out rewards to that vault even though the operator won’t be performing the assigned tasks, as it is no longer registered.

Furthermore, this vault will be unable to be slashed by the DSS because the requestSlashing function checks if the operator is registered to the DSS, which in this case, would return false and cause the function to revert. New users looking to register with operators could also be misled to deposit in the vault, believing it is registered to that DSS. 

Compared to the initially identified issue, since a change was made to allow anyone to call the finalizeUpdateVaultStakeInDSS function, this issue is now much more likely to occur.

## **Proof Of Concept:**

```solidity
    function test_add_op_unreg_dss() public {
        // register operator to dss
        addVaults();
        // request stake vaults to dss
        address requestedVault = address(vaults[0]);
        address requestedVault1 = address(vaults[1]);
        Operator.StakeUpdateRequest memory stakeUpdate =
            Operator.StakeUpdateRequest({vault: requestedVault, dss: dss, toStake: true});
        Operator.StakeUpdateRequest memory stakeUpdate1 =
            Operator.StakeUpdateRequest({vault: requestedVault1, dss: dss, toStake: true});
        vm.startPrank(operator);
        Operator.QueuedStakeUpdate memory queuedStakeUpdate = core.requestUpdateVaultStakeInDSS(stakeUpdate);
        Operator.QueuedStakeUpdate memory queuedStakeUpdate1 = core.requestUpdateVaultStakeInDSS(stakeUpdate1);
        vm.stopPrank();
        skip(8 days);
        // unregister operator from dss
        vm.prank(operator);
        core.unregisterOperatorFromDSS(dss, "");
        // finalize stake update
        skip(1 days);
        core.finalizeUpdateVaultStakeInDSS(queuedStakeUpdate);
        core.finalizeUpdateVaultStakeInDSS(queuedStakeUpdate1);
        // check if operator is unregistered from dss
        assertEq(false, core.isOperatorRegisteredToDSS(operator, dss));
        // check if vaults are staked to dss
        address[] memory operatorVaults = core.fetchVaultsStakedInDSS(operator, dss);
        assertEq(operatorVaults[0], address(vaults[0]));
        assertEq(operatorVaults[1], address(vaults[1]));
    }
```

## **Tools Used:**

- Manual analysis
- Foundry

## **Recommendation:**

Implement a check during the finalization process to ensure the operator is still registered with the DSS. This will ensure that vaults can only be staked to the operator's registered DSS's.





