# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The `SlashingHandler` will be unusable for fee-on-transfer tokens, and the `handleSlashing` function will always fail to slash this type of tokens due to a revert.

In fee-on-transfer tokens, the actual transferred amount is always less than the `amount` that was requested to be transferred, as the token contract charges its own fee.

## Proof of Concept
```solidity
    /// @notice slashes the specified amount of the token
    /// The vault needs to give approval to the slashing handler prior to slashing
    /// Pulls the assets form the vault and send them to address(0)
    /// @param token address of the token to be slashed
    /// @param amount quantity of assets to be slashed
    function handleSlashing(IERC20 token, uint256 amount) external {
        if (amount == 0) revert ZeroAmount();
        if (!_config().supportedAssets[token]) revert UnsupportedAsset();

        SafeTransferLib.safeTransferFrom(address(token), msg.sender, address(this), amount);
        // Below is where custom logic for each asset lives
        SafeTransferLib.safeTransfer(address(token), address(0), amount);
    }
```

You can see that the amount that the vault passes to be slashed (`amount`) is passed to the `safeTransferFrom` call.

If the `token` is a fee-on-transfer token, the **real amount that the `SlashingHandler` will receive after the `transferFrom` call completes** will be less than the initial `amount`.

So the `SlashingHandler` at that point has the token value of `amount - fee`.

Due to that, at the `SafeTransferLib.safeTransfer(address(token), address(0), amount);` step, the `token` contract will revert due to `SlashingHandler`'s balance being less than the `amount` passed.

## Tools Used
Manual review.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Passing the initial `amount` directly is incorrect, and, *to properly account for fee-on-transfer tokens*, it should be replaced with the following logic:
```diff
    /// @notice slashes the specified amount of the token
    /// The vault needs to give approval to the slashing handler prior to slashing
    /// Pulls the assets form the vault and send them to address(0)
    /// @param token address of the token to be slashed
    /// @param amount quantity of assets to be slashed
    function handleSlashing(IERC20 token, uint256 amount) external {
        if (amount == 0) revert ZeroAmount();
        if (!_config().supportedAssets[token]) revert UnsupportedAsset();

        SafeTransferLib.safeTransferFrom(address(token), msg.sender, address(this), amount);
        // Below is where custom logic for each asset lives
        uint realAmount = token.balanceOf(address(this)); // can also slash dust amounts that can occur in the contract outside of the function calls
        SafeTransferLib.safeTransfer(address(token), address(0), realAmount);
    }
```


