```solidity
    function fetchEarmarkedStakes(SlashRequest memory slashingMetadata)
        internal
        view
        returns (uint256[] memory earmarkedStakes)
    {
        earmarkedStakes = new uint256[](slashingMetadata.vaults.length);
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < slashingMetadata.vaults.length; ++i) {
            earmarkedStakes[i] = Math.mulDiv(
                slashingMetadata.slashPercentagesWad[i],
                IKarakBaseVault(slashingMetadata.vaults[i]).totalAssets(),
                Constants.MAX_SLASHING_PERCENT_WAD
            );
        }
    }
```

After the `SLASHING_VETO_WINDOW` is passed in which such slashing request is not canceled by the slashing veto committee, the following `Core.finalizeSlashing` function can be called to further call the `SlasherLib.finalizeSlashing` and `Vault.slashAssets` functions to slash `queuedSlashing.earmarkedStakes[i]`, which is the token amount to be slashed calculated by the previous `Core.requestSlashing` function call, from the vault.

